# Copy this file to `.env` and change what you need. `.env` is never committed.
#
# The client reads only two settings, and BOTH HAVE SENSIBLE DEFAULTS — the app
# runs with no .env file at all. They are here for the cases where the defaults
# are wrong.

# ---- Where the API is, in development only ---------------------------------
# `npm run dev` serves the site on 5173 and forwards every /api call to this
# address, so the browser only ever talks to one origin and there is no CORS to
# configure. Change it if the API is running on another port or another machine
# (an office PC pointing at the server on someone else's desk, say).
# Not used in a build: on Vercel the forwarding is done by client/vercel.json.
VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:4000

# ---- Where the API is, in the built site -----------------------------------
# Left blank, the app calls /api on its own origin, which is what you want:
# client/vercel.json rewrites that across to the API project, so the browser
# stays same-origin and no CORS header has to be right.
#
# Set it ONLY to point the built site straight at another API — a staging
# server, or a local build talking to the live API. A full address, no trailing
# slash, e.g. https://stemvision-api.vercel.app/api
VITE_API_URL=
